## Decoder limits and error shape

A lower byte limit returns the same typed Error struct used by other fallible calls.

Decode with a deliberately small byte limit and read the stable error fields.

```elixir
{:error, %AgentBlueprintProtocol.Error{} = limit_error} =
  AgentBlueprintProtocol.decode_blueprint(blueprint_bytes, %{bytes: 16})

%{code: limit_error.code, subject: limit_error.subject, detail: limit_error.detail}
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{code: {:ceiling, :bytes}, detail: nil, subject: []}
```

